    {
      "short_id": "short261",
      "angle": "The dissent answered the majority's preference for mail with stolen mailboxes and evidence it considered too thin.",
      "avoids": "No composite people, invented aftermath, guessed vote, or claim that removal occurred in these tenants' cases.",
      "funnel_question_left_for_longform": "If neither the door nor the mail is perfectly reliable, what process is enough?",
      "loop": true,
      "loop_join": "The final line returns to the dissent's mailbox image from the hook.",
      "era": "Louisville, Kentucky, early 1980s",
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "L1",
          "text": "The majority said this posted notice failed. The dissent answered with an image: unattended mailboxes, it wrote, are subject to plunder by thieves.",
          "delivery": "intense",
          "source_lines": [
            "The dissent offered the counter-image that has outlived everything else in it."
          ],
          "claims": []
        },
        {
          "id": "L2",
          "text": "That argument belonged to the dissent. A mailed letter can be stolen or misdelivered, while posting at least reaches the tenant's door.",
          "delivery": "building",
          "source_lines": [
            "That is a real argument."
          ],
          "claims": []
        },
        {
          "id": "L3",
          "text": "The dissent said the majority preferred the Postal Service without proving that mail worked better than a notice fixed to the home.",
          "delivery": "building",
          "source_lines": [
            "The majority never proved the mails were better."
          ],
          "claims": []
        },
        {
          "id": "L4",
          "text": "It also attacked the evidence: scant and conflicting testimony from only a handful of Kentucky process servers.",
          "delivery": "building",
          "source_lines": [
            "Then the charge."
          ],
          "claims": []
        },
        {
          "id": "L5",
          "text": "The dissent counted at least eleven States that allowed notice solely by posting or by leaving it at the residence.",
          "delivery": "building",
          "source_lines": [
            "It listed them in a footnote. At least eleven."
          ],
          "claims": []
        },
        {
          "id": "L6",
          "text": "The majority's answer was narrower: whatever posting does elsewhere, on this record it did not reliably provide actual notice.",
          "delivery": "building",
          "source_lines": [
            "The majority never proved the mails were better. It proved this door was worse."
          ],
          "claims": []
        },
        {
          "id": "L7",
          "text": "No vote tally is printed in the opinion, so this is not a story about a guessed five-to-four or six-to-three split.",
          "delivery": "building",
          "source_lines": [
            "The majority's opinion does not answer that one."
          ],
          "claims": []
        },
        {
          "id": "L8",
          "text": "It is a dispute about imperfect delivery systems, ending where the dissent began: with a letter sitting in an unattended mailbox.",
          "delivery": "calm",
          "source_lines": [
            "That is a real argument."
          ],
          "claims": []
        }
      ],
